✅ Q14 — Find the First Number That Appears More Than Once

🎗️ 14.1 Problem Statement

You are given a List<Integer> containing positive, negative, and zero values.
Using Java Streams, find the first number that appears more than once in the list.

Your solution should:

👉 Use the Stream API.
🔴 Return the result as an Integer.
🔴 Preserve the original encounter order.
🔴 Correctly handle positive and negative integers.
🔴 Correctly handle duplicate values.
🔴 Correctly handle zero.
🔴 Correctly handle an empty list.
🔴 Return an appropriate result when no duplicate number exists.

🎗️ 14.2 Input / Output

👉 Input List

Use this exact list in your Java program:
List<Integer> numbersList = Arrays.asList(10, 25, 10, -5, 40, 25, 15, -5, 30, 25);

👉 Expected Output : 10

Because:

10  → appears 2 times ✅ ← First duplicate
25  → appears 3 times
-5  → appears 2 times
40  → appears 1 time
15  → appears 1 time
30  → appears 1 time

The first number whose total occurrence is greater than one is: 10

🎗️ 14.3 Your Task

Write the Java Stream solution.

You can provide:

🔴 Your primary approach
🔴 Any alternative approaches — Streams only
🔴 Your thoughts about empty-list behavior
🔴 How you preserve encounter order
🔴 Time and space complexity, if you want to attempt those too.